     "result_text_tail": "change-rate effects.\n  - The tariff rise is applied from 2027, the harsher case.\n- **Stall case:** the only figure I estimated myself. It holds sales at 12 times the June 2026 pilot month at the pilot's 28% ad cost, and its basis is shown on the slide.\n\n**Checks**\n- 293 numbers, every one traced to a quoted line of the briefing pack or a formula that recalculates live in the workbook. There are no \"?\" placeholders.\n- A separate reviewer re-traced the title and summary numbers from the pack and found them correct. It caught one false summary line and four loose wordings, and I fixed all of them.\n- Of the 12 leaf hypotheses, 5 were confirmed, 4 refuted and 3 revised.\n- Because the pack is the only source, no number has a second independent source and none of them can reach the workbook's top grade.\n\n**Remaining QA warnings, left on purpose**\n- Onsoo's 4% awareness sits beside the sell-through chart because it is what places Onsoo in the lowest band.\n- \"Four months\" of inventory is written as a word in the pack.\n- Three hypotheses the board can't influence (market growth, the tariff, the Amazon lift from retail) stay in because they decide the answer.\n\nNext, I can switch the theme or rerun the case with your own assumptions, such as a different ad cost or launch date.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `onsoo-us-entry.pptx`: 42 slides, 25 of them content\n- `onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx`: source and formula for every number\n- `onsoo-us-entry.json`: the deck's spec, for future edits"
